  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Helpers overlap briefly at a shift change and can use a shared list of unfinished tasks.\", \"decision\": \"How should helpers hand over unfinished tasks?\", \"goal\": \"Keep books moving and make the afternoon service easier to use without excluding readers who arrive without an appointment.\", \"problem\": \"A small library becomes crowded during afternoon pickups and returns. It has a request sheet, adjustable pickup windows, a few trained helpers, labeled shelves, and enough room to separate several activities. Staff want a practical plan that preserves walk-in access. Each decision below concerns a different part of the service; none requires exclusive use of all helpers or space.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nBoth helpers mark unfinished tasks on the shared list as they occur, then review only unresolved entries during the overlap. The handover focuses on work that still needs attention.\nThe outgoing helper writes the unfinished-task list before the overlap and explains it to the incoming helper. The handover starts from a prepared record.\nThe incoming helper reviews the work during the overlap and writes the unfinished-task list with the outgoing helper. The new helper checks understanding while the record is made."
    }
  ],
